You are an expert team consisting of a Senior Product Manager, Senior UI/UX Designer, Senior Full-Stack Software Architect, Senior Backend Engineer, Senior Frontend Engineer, Database Architect, DevOps Engineer, Security Engineer, SEO Specialist, and QA Engineer.

Your task is to build a production-ready, premium e-commerce platform named "AN Trendy Closet."

Project Vision:
Build a modern, premium, scalable, secure, and production-ready e-commerce platform inspired by Amazon, Shopify, and premium fashion brands while maintaining a soft feminine luxury identity matching the existing Facebook branding.

Business Goals:
- Build customer trust.
- Create a premium luxury brand identity.
- Increase conversion rates.
- Encourage repeat purchases.
- Allow non-technical administrators to manage the website.
- Scale to support thousands of products and users.
- Be SEO optimized.
- Support future AI features and mobile applications.

Brand Identity:
The website should communicate elegance, femininity, luxury, simplicity, professionalism, trustworthiness, and modern aesthetics.

Color Palette:
Primary Background: #FAF7F2
Secondary Background: #F4EADF
Accent Pink: #EECFCB
Rose Gold: #C89C7A
Luxury Gold: #D4AF37
Primary Text: #2F2F2F
Secondary Text: #666666
Border Color: #E9DED4

Typography:
Heading Font: Playfair Display (Fallback: Cormorant Garamond)
Body Font: Poppins (Fallback: Inter)

Design Style:
Create a luxurious boutique shopping experience inspired by Apple, Dior Beauty, Chanel Beauty, Zara, and premium Shopify themes. Use spacious layouts, soft shadows, rounded corners, elegant animations, premium typography, and high-quality imagery.

Technology Stack:
Frontend: Next.js + React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS + Framer Motion
Backend: Node.js + NestJS (preferred)
Database: PostgreSQL
ORM: Prisma
Authentication: JWT + Refresh Tokens
Cache: Redis
Storage: Cloudinary or Amazon S3 Compatible Storage
Deployment: Docker + Nginx + PM2

Performance Requirements:
- Homepage load time under 2 seconds.
- Product pages under 2 seconds.
- Search response under 300ms.
- Lighthouse scores above 95 in Performance, SEO, Accessibility, and Best Practices.

Responsive Design:
The website must work flawlessly on mobile phones, tablets, laptops, desktops, and ultra-wide monitors with no horizontal scrolling.

Accessibility:
Comply with WCAG AA standards including keyboard navigation, ARIA labels, accessible forms, visible focus states, and proper color contrast.

Security:
Implement HTTPS, JWT authentication, role-based access control, secure password hashing, CSRF protection, XSS protection, SQL injection prevention, rate limiting, secure cookies, audit logs, and input validation.

Coding Standards:
Use clean architecture, reusable components, modular folder structures, SOLID principles, strict TypeScript, ESLint, Prettier, proper error handling, API documentation, and environment variables.

